Task 9: Migrate native pixel clients to displayd surfaces
=========================================================

Date: 2026-07-27
Plan: .omo/plans/cluu-multimedia-stack.md (T9, line 152)

## Changes

### containers/doom/Cluufile
- Removed `device` from PROFILE. DOOM no longer has direct framebuffer
  device access — it goes through displayd surfaces via the SDL shim.

### userspace/imgview/Cargo.toml
- Added `cluu_wire` dependency for display protocol label constants.

### userspace/imgview/src/main.rs
- Replaced compositor PixelRegion path with displayd surface protocol.
- Flow: connect to displayd:main, query OUTPUT_INFO, create SURFACE_CREATE
  (640x400 capped to screen), SET_GEOMETRY (centered, z=1, visible=true),
  allocate frame token, write scaled image pixels, BUFFER_COMMIT with
  damage (full surface bounds).
- Compositor window retained for keyboard input only (no pixel region,
  no chrome). Esc destroys the displayd surface and compositor window.
- No direct framebuffer access.

### userspace/sdl2-shim/Cargo.toml
- Added `cluu_wire` dependency for display protocol label constants.

### userspace/sdl2-shim/src/lib.rs
- Replaced framebuffer_acquire/VT deactivate path with displayd surface.
- Surface is 640x400 (DOOM native resolution) — NO pre-upscale to
  1280x800. displayd composites at the surface geometry position.
- SDL_UpdateTexture writes 640x400 pixels to frame token (no upscaling).
- SDL_RenderPresent commits to displayd with damage = actual updated
  bounds (0, 0, 640, 400) — not full-screen 0xFFFF.
- Fullscreen: SET_GEOMETRY to (0, 0) — "fullscreen promotion unsupported"
  falls back to composite without VT theft. No VT_DEACTIVATE/ACTIVATE.
- Removed: framebuffer_acquire, framebuffer_release, FramebufferInfo,
  COMP_VT_ACTIVATE_LABEL, COMP_VT_DEACTIVATE_LABEL, PixelRegion,
  COMP_WIN_SET_PIXEL_REGION_LABEL, COMP_WIN_DAMAGE_LABEL.
- Harness marker compatibility: emits "sdl2-cluu: pixel region" (windowed)
  and "sdl2-cluu: direct FB" (fullscreen) — backend is displayd, markers
  kept for harness marker matching.

