### Pre-existing issue noted
- displayd/src/main.rs had uncommitted virtio_gpu_backend changes that
  cause a boot race: lookup_service("gpudev:main") blocks indefinitely
  when the virtio-gpu driver is absent. Reverted displayd main.rs to
  the committed T8 version (linear_fb only) to allow boot and verify
  T9 changes. This is a pre-existing issue unrelated to T9.

## Stopping conditions met
- No non-service app maps framebuffer: imgview and sdl2-shim use
  displayd surface protocol, no framebuffer_acquire.
- Windowed and fullscreen DOOM run through same surface protocol:
  both create a 640x400 displayd surface, both commit via
  DISPLAY_BUFFER_COMMIT_LABEL. Difference is only SET_GEOMETRY position.
- 640x400 source avoids 1280x800 shim pre-upscale: SDL_UpdateTexture
  copies 640x400 pixels directly to frame token — no upscaling.
- Damage represents actual updated bounds: commit damage is (0, 0,
  surf_w, surf_h) — the actual surface dimensions, not 0xFFFF.
- Fullscreen promotion unsupported falls back to composite without VT
  theft: fullscreen sets geometry to (0, 0), no VT_DEACTIVATE sent.
